    "https://jobmarket.unibocconi.eu/?id=987": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Dept. Economics",
      "description": "Closing Date: 15/11/2026 Posted Date: 25/09/2026 Department: Economics  Via Sarfatti, 25 - 20136 Milano, Italia unibocconi.it Call for two Assistant Professor Positions in Economics for Junior Candidates Bocconi University invites applications for two tenure-track positions at the Assistant Professor level in the Department of Economics, starting in Fall 2027. Key information: • This early-career position is intended for candidates whose PhD in Economics, Finance, or a closely related field was conferred on or after 1 September 2023. For candidates with documented career interruptions that prevented research activity (e.g., parental leave, long-term illness, or comparable circumstances), the cutoff date will be moved back by the length of the interruption. • Applications are welcome from candidates working in any field of economics. • The appointment is for an eight-year tenure-track contract. Candidates may be considered for promotion to a tenured position at any time before the end of the contract, subject to successful evaluation. • Compensation and teaching responsibilities are competitive with those offered by other leading European institutions, with a minimum gross annual salary of 100,000 euros. The final remuneration package will be determined based on the candidate's experience, qualifications and overall professional profile, in accordance with the University's principles of equity, transparency and non-discrimination governing its compensation policies. • Candidates should demonstrate a strong record of, or clear potential for excellence in research and teaching. • Applications must be submitted through the online form available at: https://jobmarket.unibocconi.eu/?id=987 • The application deadline is Sunday, November 15, 2026, at 23:59 Central European Summer Time (CEST). • Candidates are required to provide the contact details of three highly qualified academic referees. Each referee will automatically receive an email from the system with instructions to upload their reference letter directly. Additional information: • Applicants whose Ph.D. was conferred before September 1, 2023, should apply through Bocconi University’s separate call for Experienced Assistant Professor positions in Economics, which is available following this link: https://jobmarket.unibocconi.eu/?id=976. "
    },
    "https://jobmarket.unibocconi.eu/?id=936": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Dept. Law, Giur-17/A Filosofia Del Diritto",
      "description": "Closing Date: 08/11/2026 Posted Date: 22/09/2026 Department: Law  Milano, 22/09/2026, prot. n. 226083 [Cod. riferimento: AP] COMPETITION FOR THE CONFERRAL OF N. 1 FIXED-TERM PRIVATE LAW CONTRACT AS “ASSISTANT PROFESSOR” IN THE “ANGELO SRAFFA” DEPARTMENT OF LEGAL STUDIES OF UNIVERSITÀ COMMERCIALE “LUIGI BOCCONI” OF MILAN Article 1 Università Commerciale “Luigi Bocconi” of Milan, according to former article 24 of Law 30 December 2010, n. 240 amended by Law n. 79 of 29 June 2022, and using the methods explained in its “ Regulation governing Bocconi University’s procedures for selection of Assistant Professors”, emanated with Rectoral Decree n. 1 05 of 21 December 2022 , announces a competition for the conferral of 1 fixed-term private law contract as Assistant Professor, to carry out research, teaching and assistance for students, with the following characteristics: Type of contract : Assistant Professor contract, former article 24 of Law 240/2010 , amended by Law n. 79 of 29 June 2022 Duration: six-year contract Starting date: 1st February 2027 Department: “Angelo Sraffa” Department of Legal Studies Scientific-Disciplinary Group: 12/GIUR-17 PHILOSOPHY OF LAW Scientific-Disciplinary Sector: GIUR-17/A Philosophy of Law Article 2 Admission Requirements Candidates for the Assistant Professor position must be scholars with a PhD or equivalent degree, carried out in Italy or abroad. University professors and researchers who have already been employed under a permanent contract, even if having ceased service, are excluded from participation in the selection procedure, as are persons who have already served for three years or more under a contract as tenure-track fixed-term researcher referred to in point 3 of Law 240/2010, 2022 version. Relations or kin, up to and including 4th grade, with a professor who is part of the Department asking for the vacancy, as well as with the Rector, General Director or a component of the University Board cannot apply. Article 3 Applications Applications according to the on-line application form, must be sent electronically via the website https://jobmarket.unibocconi.eu/?id=936 by 2 3:59, 8 November 2026 (Italian time). The following documents must be attached to the electronic application: a) a scientific curriculum comprising the following sections: - education - list of titles and publications - teaching experience - presentations at seminars and conferences - institutional roles; b) a “ Research Statement ” with a maximum length of 3,000 words , that describes the candidate’s objectives and experiences in research and in activities of service to the scientific community; c) a 1,000-word “Letter of intent”, describing the candidate past e xperiences and reasons for applying; d) all publications and works that the candidate intend s to submit for comparative evaluation, up to a maximum of twelve attachments, uploaded in descending order of importance based on the candidate’s own evaluation; e) a list of three highly qualified academic referees willing to provid e a reference letter. The reference letters will only be requested if the candidate is selected for the oral interview. For any problem related to uploading the files, the candidate can contact faculty@unibocconi.it. If the candidate has any other public administration roles , they must send a declaration stating the type of position and role currently being carried out to faculty@unibocconi.it. Any possible externally paid roles may only be carried out after authorization by the Academic Bodies of Bocconi University, according to the current regulations of the University. Article 4 Selection Procedure To carry out the selection, the Department uses the Junior Hiring Committee, nominated by the competent organ of the Department according to the Department Regulations, and chaired by a Full Professor as Head of the Junior Job Market, having consulted the Dean of the Faculty. The composition of the Junior Hiring Committee will be such as to ensure the presence of a Bocconi tenured full professor affiliated to the same Scientific Disciplinary Group indicated in Article 1 of this Call, and two external full or associate professors belonging to the same Scientific-Disciplinary Group or to a like Group. For the hiring via the National and International job market, the evaluation of the applications will be carried out by the Junior Hiring Committee, that will draw up a short list of candidates. The short list of candi dates to be interviewed must be between 10 and 20 percent of the applications, and in any case the number of interviews cannot be smaller than the minimum between 6 and the number of applications, if the applications are deemed eligible according to the Scientific-Disciplinary Group advertised, as reported by attachment C of MD n. 639 of 2 May 2024. Each selected candidate will be interviewed in person or via conference call, according to International Job Market practices , to assess their teaching and research abilities and interest in covering the Assistant Professor position. Deserving candidates may also be invited to the University to carry out a series of interviews in the Department and to give a seminar based on their research (fly out). These interviews as well as the seminar may be carried out via conference call. At the end of the selection process the Department Board, heard the Dean of the Faculty, will write an overall evaluation for each selected candidate, forming a table of eligible candidates. Following the proposal of the Department the University has the possibility to make an offer to eligible candidates, which must explain: the contract type, teaching load required, requested scientific commitments in terms of minimum publications requested and proposed salary. Salaries for Assistant Professors start from € 50,000 per year. The final salary offer may be adjusted according to the actual seniority of the successful candidate, in accordance with the objective and non -discriminatory criteria adopted by the University. The offer letter must also indicate the deadline by which the candidate must communicate their acceptance of the offer. If the candidate accepts the offer, the University will draw up a fixed term, private law contract. As established by its 2026-30 Strategic Plan, Bocconi University is committed to pursuing its chief objectives in research and instruction in a physical and intellectual environment in which all – students, faculty, staff – receive, and offer to others, equal opportunity, dignity and treatment, irrespective of gender, sexual orientation, ethnicity, religion, age or economic condition. To this purpose the present Call , together with all of Bocconi University’s Regulations for selection, will respect the crosscutting principles prescribed by EU Regulation 2021/241, in particular the principles of gender equality, protection and valorization of young people and of the overcoming of regional disparities. Article 5 Rights and Duties of the Assistant Professor The Assistant Professor contract lasts for six years and starts from 1st February 2027. The Assistant Professor will have the following commitments: - Teaching activity, in their given scientific sector, also assuming the responsibility for coordination of multi -class courses, as agreed annually by the Academic Council, for a number of classroom hours equal to 96 hours/year, preparation of teaching material and assistance to students and checking of their knowledge. - Research activity, also carrying out the scientific coordination thereof, within research projects developed by the Department of referral, as well as within the structure of research centers within the University, with the aim of producing an adequate number of scientific publications in prestigious sites, or considered to be such by the University, before the maximum duration of the current contract. Mid-term Evaluation . At the start of the fourth year the activity conducted by the Assistant Professor will be evaluated, according to the following parameters: - For the teaching activity, the Department considers the fulfillment of teaching obligations and assesses individual performance in accordance with procedures established by the University. - For the research activity, the Department evaluates the scientific works produced, including the working papers, ascertains whether they have been credibly submitted to prestigious journals, accords positive value to responses of the “Revise and resubmit” type and to any publication thereof. Participation as speaker at international conferences of exceptional prestige will also be taken into consideration. The outcome of such evaluation is formalized and communicated to both the Assistant Professor and the Dean of the Faculty. In the event of a positive mid-term evaluation the Department may activate the procedure for tenure during the contract’s second three -year period. In such case the following parameters will be adopted: - For the teaching activity: fulfillment of teaching obligations and assessment of individual performance in accordance with procedures established by the University. - For the research activity: evaluation of research projects conducted and ascertainment of the number of scientific publications produced. In particular, for conferral of tenure as Associate Professor, an adequate number of scientific publications in prestigious venues or deemed equivalent thereto by the University, and positive evaluations of the activities of teaching and service to students effected over the entire term of the contract are required. The University will also evaluate the position of the Assistant Professor in the scientific community of reference through letters of assessment requested to referees, in part independent and in part indicated by the Department concerned. Article 6 Definition of the Relationship The following elements will be subject to negotiation between the University administration and the winning candidate, according to the preceding articles: 1) the economic conditions, within the limits imposed by the University Board; in any case the economic conditions cannot be less than the Ministerial tables dictated for "
    },
