      "title": "Associate Professor, Dept. Social and Political Sciences, Full or Associate Professor position",
      "description": "Closing Date: 18/10/2026 Posted Date: 28/08/2026 Department: Social and Political Sciences P iazza Sraﬀa 11 - 20136 Milano, Italia unibocconi.it Bocconi University, Department of Social and Poli�cal Sciences Compara�ve Poli�cs, Open Rank The Department of Social and Political Sciences at Bocconi University is inviting applications for a n open-rank faculty position in Political Science, speci�ically within the sub�ield of comparative politics (with an emphasis on either mass behavior, political economy, or political institutions). An Assistant Professor (junior) position would be tenure-track; an Associate or Full Professor (senior) position would be tenured. The appointment begins on September 1, 2027. To complement the existing strengths and pro�ile of the department, candidates engaged in research employing rigorous quantitative analysis are highly preferred. Junior candidates should show evidence of a promising research agenda, while senior candidates should possess a high-impact and internationally visible record of research. All candidates should be doing work that engages with multiple �ields of study in the department—political science, applied economics, public administration and health, sociology and demograph y, and economic history. Candidates should also be able to teach courses in comparative politics at the undergraduate and graduate levels, speci�ically in the university’s undergraduate program in International Politics and Government, its master's program in Politics and Policy Analysis, and its PhD program in Social and Political Sciences. Bocconi University is a leading European research and teaching institution in economics, social sciences, management and related disciplines. In the 2025 QS World University Ranking of Social Science s and Management programs, Bocconi ranked 4th in Europe and 12th worldwide. The Department of Social and Political Sciences provides an ideal interdisciplinary research environment. It comprises approximately 60 tenured or tenure-track faculty members who share an interest in policy-relevant research, addressing questions on numer ous world challenges, such as inequality, government responsiveness and accountabilit y, corruption and organized crime, environmental sustainabilit y, global health, and international cooperation . Bocconi is located in Italy's most vibrant cente r, Milan, a historic, cosmopolitan and international city in a metropolitan area of 3 million that is well connected to the rest of Europe and the world. Knowledge of Italian is not required. Terms of employment are competitive and salaries for Associate Professors in political science start from € 100,000. The �inal salary offer may be adjusted according to the actual seniority of the successful candidate, in accordance with the objective and non-discriminatory criteria adopted by the University. Applications should be received by October 18, 2026. Applicants must submit (1) a current curriculum vitae, (2) a job market paper (and up to four other published papers), (3) a cover letter, and (4) teaching and research statements via the on-l ine form using PDF attachments at www.unibocconi.eu/jobmarket. Additionally, junior applicants should have at least three academic letters of reference submitted by referees via www.unibocconi.eu/jobmarket, while senior applicants should provide a list of at least three references. Junior applicants must successfully defend their PhD thesis by no later than October 18, 2026 to receive a �inal offer of employment. Bocconi University is committed to increasing the diversity of its facult y. Applications are particularly welcome from women and members of groups who are under-represented in academic posts. "
